# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is NOT in version control, and why
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The point of this repo is your CODE + your small user-state JSON, so that any
# future edit is a reviewable diff and a rollback is one command. Everything
# below is either huge, regenerable, or machine-local.
#
# NOTE: `data/puzzles.sqlite` is 2.4 GB. It is NOT committed, and it must never
# live in a cloud-sync folder (Drive/iCloud/Dropbox) either — syncing a live
# SQLite file can corrupt it, and it is rebuildable from source whenever you
# need it (`node scripts/build-sqlite.mjs`).

# --- big + regenerable -----------------------------------------------------
# Keep the docs, drop the database itself.
/data/*
!/data/README.md
node_modules/
/.next/
/out/
/build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Lichess source data (~1.9 GB) -----------------------------------------
# These are the RAW downloads used to build data/puzzles.sqlite. Re-downloadable
# at any time (see scripts/build-sqlite.mjs), and far too big for a code repo.
/lichess_db_puzzle.csv
/lichess_db_puzzle.csv.zst
/filtered_puzzles.csv
*.csv.zst

# --- dependency + tooling noise -------------------------------------------
.pnp
.pnp.js
.npm
.eslintcache
coverage/

# --- machine-local ---------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*.pem
.vercel
next-env.d.ts

# --- env / secrets (never commit these) ------------------------------------
.env
.env*.local

# --- local scratch ---------------------------------------------------------
/tmp/
*.log
# Throwaway scripts agent runs create and delete mid-flight; they break `git add`
# if a scan catches them vanishing.
scripts/_tmp-*
scripts/.tmp-*
